-- title:
--   The divisor rε+r'z₀ over R and over A
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $c\colon C\to\operatorname{Spec}R$ a separated morphism of schemes and $U\subseteq C$ an open subscheme such that the composite of the inclusion $U\hookrightarrow C$ with $c$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$. Let $\varepsilon$ be a morphism $\operatorname{Spec}R\to C$ with $\varepsilon\circ$-composite equal to the identity (a section of $c$) whose set-theoretic image lies in $U$, let $A$ be a finite faithfully flat $R$-algebra, $B_0$ a finite étale $R$-algebra, $d\in\mathbb N$, and $\varphi_0\colon A\otimes_R B_0\xrightarrow{\sim}A^{d}$ an isomorphism of $A$-algebras. Let $z_0\colon\operatorname{Spec}B_0\to C$ be a closed immersion with $z_0$ followed by $c$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R\to B_0$ and with image in $U$, and let $r,r',\rho\in\mathbb N$ with $\rho=r+r'd$. Then there exist a closed immersion $z_A\colon\operatorname{Spec}(A\otimes_R B_0)\to (C\times_R\operatorname{Spec}A)\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A}\operatorname{Spec}A$ whose projection to $C$ agrees with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $B_0\to A\otimes_R B_0$ followed by $z_0$ and whose projection to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $A\to A\otimes_R B_0$, together with relative effective Cartier divisors $E$ for $c$ of rank $\rho$ over $\operatorname{Spec}R$ and $E'$ for the base change $C\times_R\operatorname{Spec}A\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ of rank $\rho$ over $\operatorname{Spec}A$ — that is, quasi-coherent ideal sheaf data on the relevant fibre products whose closed subscheme is finite, flat and locally of finite presentation over the base with fibre rank $\rho$ everywhere — such that: the support of $E$ lies over $U$ and that of $E'$ over the preimage of $U$ under the first projection $C\times_R\operatorname{Spec}A\to C$; $E$'s ideal is the $r$-th power of the kernel ideal of the section induced by $\varepsilon$ times the $r'$-th power of the kernel ideal of the lift of $z_0$; $E'$'s ideal is the $r$-th power of the kernel ideal of the section induced by the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $A$ times the $r'$-th power of the kernel ideal of $z_A$; for every scheme $T$ and every $t\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ the ideal of the pullback of $E'$ along $t$ is invertible, i.e. locally on affine basic opens generated by a single non-zero-divisor; for all $t\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}A$, $t'\colon T'\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ and every $A$-morphism $\psi\colon T'\to T$ over them, the pullback along the induced map of fibre products of the line bundle (the inverse module of the ideal) of $E'_{T}$ is isomorphic to that of $E'_{T'}$; and for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$, every $s_\Omega\colon\operatorname{Spec}\Omega\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ and every isomorphism $\varphi$ between $(C\times_R\operatorname{Spec}A)\times_A\operatorname{Spec}\Omega$ and $C\times_R\operatorname{Spec}\Omega$ compatible with the projections to $C$, the pullback along $\varphi$ of the line bundle of $E$ pulled back to $\operatorname{Spec}\Omega$ is isomorphic to the line bundle of $E'$ pulled back along $s_\Omega$.
--
--   This is the packaged construction of the polarising divisor $r\varepsilon+r'z_0$ on a smooth patch of a relative curve, simultaneously over the base $\operatorname{Spec}R$ and over a finite faithfully flat cover $\operatorname{Spec}A$ splitting the étale block $z_0$, together with the invertibility, base-change and geometric-fibre comparisons of the associated line bundles. It is used in the per-patch assembly of representability for the relative sub-Picard functor, in [`AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.forall_prime_exists_representsRelSubPic_algEquivZeroCut_baseChange_away_of_smoothLocus_of_twoGluedSmoothCurveDegenerations`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.forall_prime_exists_representsRelSubPic_algEquivZeroCut_baseChange_away_of_smoothLocus_of_twoGluedSmoothCurveDegenerations).
